From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Skip vkSetLatencySleepModeNV for managed swapchains.

Managed cross-process swapchains (wineland child rendering) have no host
swapchain, so their host handle is VK_NULL_HANDLE. The wineland series
already skips vkLatencySleepNV, vkSetLatencyMarkerNV and
vkGetLatencyTimingsNV for them, but vkSetLatencySleepModeNV comes from
the separately applied NVIDIA Reflex patch (83-nv_low_latency_wine),
which is applied after that series, and still passed the null handle to
the driver.

Arc Raiders creates a managed swapchain when its window is unfocused
while a level loads. vkd3d-proton then sets the latency sleep mode on
it, and the NVIDIA driver crashes on the null swapchain
(libnvidia-glcore + 0x304c75, "vkSetLatencySleepModeNV Exception
0xc0000005 in Unix call").

Return VK_SUCCESS without calling the driver, as vkLatencySleepNV does.
The device's low_latency_enabled flag is still updated.

Follow-up to 0087-winevulkan-Skip-time-domain-queries-for-managed-swapchains.

Bug: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/891
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/win32u/vulkan.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -3817,6 +3817,9 @@
     sleep_mode_info_host.lowLatencyBoost = pSleepModeInfo->lowLatencyBoost;
     sleep_mode_info_host.minimumIntervalUs = pSleepModeInfo->minimumIntervalUs;
 
+    /* Managed swapchains have no host swapchain to set the mode on. */
+    if (!vk_swapchain || vk_swapchain->managed) return VK_SUCCESS;
+
     return vk_device->p_vkSetLatencySleepModeNV(vk_device->host.device, vk_swapchain->obj.host.swapchain, &sleep_mode_info_host);
 }
 
